WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.118
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:08.607
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.907 --> 00:00:14.590
Unit twelve: Body Paragraphs. Today you will develop each main point in a body paragraph.

4
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.623
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:21.683
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:23.238
Body.

7
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.389
Body means the middle part of an essay.

8
00:00:26.983 --> 00:00:29.192
The body has three paragraphs.

9
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:32.285
Your turn. Say: Body.

10
00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:35.995
Body.

11
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:37.879
Main point.

12
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:41.649
Main point means the key idea of a paragraph.

13
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.470
Each paragraph has one main point.

14
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:47.422
Your turn. Say: Main point.

15
00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:51.395
Main point.

16
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.244
Evidence.

17
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.911
Evidence means facts that support an idea.

18
00:00:57.517 --> 00:00:59.203
Add evidence to your point.

19
00:00:59.817 --> 00:01:02.028
Your turn. Say: Evidence.

20
00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:05.763
Evidence.

21
00:01:06.517 --> 00:01:07.692
Explain.

22
00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:10.915
Explain means to make an idea clear.

23
00:01:11.517 --> 00:01:13.319
Explain why it matters.

24
00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:16.337
Your turn. Say: Explain.

25
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.549
Explain.

26
00:01:21.283 --> 00:01:22.342
Furthermore.

27
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.477
Furthermore means in addition (formal).

28
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:27.711
Furthermore, it saves money.

29
00:01:28.317 --> 00:01:30.818
Your turn. Say: Furthermore.

30
00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:34.691
Furthermore.

31
00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:36.556
For instance.

32
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:40.002
For instance means used to give an example.

33
00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:42.442
For instance, in Phnom Penh.

34
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:45.482
Your turn. Say: For instance.

35
00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:49.462
For instance.

36
00:01:50.217 --> 00:01:51.276
Transition.

37
00:01:52.283 --> 00:01:55.072
Transition means a word that connects paragraphs.

38
00:01:55.683 --> 00:01:57.462
Use a transition word.

39
00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:01.051
Your turn. Say: Transition.

40
00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:04.959
Transition.

41
00:02:05.717 --> 00:02:06.671
Relevant.

42
00:02:07.683 --> 00:02:10.252
Relevant means closely connected to the topic.

43
00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:12.559
Use relevant examples.

44
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.686
Your turn. Say: Relevant.

45
00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:19.407
Relevant.

46
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.595
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.891
Visal, what goes in a body paragraph?

48
00:02:27.983 --> 00:02:37.381
Each body paragraph has a topic sentence, evidence and an explanation. Use PEE: point, evidence, explain.

49
00:02:38.483 --> 00:02:39.833
How do I give evidence?

50
00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:49.211
Use facts, numbers or real examples. For instance, trees in a city can lower the temperature by several degrees.

51
00:02:50.317 --> 00:02:52.235
How do I connect paragraphs?

52
00:02:53.350 --> 00:03:00.449
Use transitions such as furthermore, in addition and however. They guide the reader from one idea to the next.

53
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.634
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:07.551
Grammar focus: Point, evidence, explain.

55
00:03:07.851 --> 00:03:08.933
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:15.335
Trees cool the city. For instance, streets with trees are cooler. This makes life more comfortable.

57
00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:21.784
Trees clean the air. For example, leaves catch dust. As a result, people breathe better.

58
00:03:22.733 --> 00:03:28.671
Use point, evidence and explanation in every body paragraph. Link paragraphs with transitions.

59
00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:33.160
Be careful! Don't say: For instance, is a good example.

60
00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:38.040
Say: For instance, it is a good example.

61
00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.829
Add a full clause.

62
00:03:40.633 --> 00:03:43.483
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:45.767
A Strong Paragraph.

64
00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:48.473
Bopha's first body paragraph is about heat.

65
00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.849
She states her point in the first sentence.

66
00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:55.216
She adds evidence from a news report.

67
00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.571
She explains why the evidence matters.

68
00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:02.123
Furthermore, she links to the next paragraph.

69
00:04:03.233 --> 00:04:07.316
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.184
The body is the blank of an essay.

71
00:04:10.484 --> 00:04:13.337
A, middle. B, end. C, cover.

72
00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.737
The answer is A: middle.

73
00:04:19.883 --> 00:04:21.906
PEE means point, evidence, blank.

74
00:04:22.206 --> 00:04:25.534
A, end. B, explain. C, enjoy.

75
00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.123
The answer is B: explain.

76
00:04:32.283 --> 00:04:34.051
For instance gives an blank.

77
00:04:34.351 --> 00:04:37.586
A, order. B, answer. C, example.

78
00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:43.249
The answer is C: example.

79
00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:46.336
A transition connects blank.

80
00:04:46.636 --> 00:04:50.058
A, ideas. B, chairs. C, cities.

81
00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.472
The answer is A: ideas.

82
00:04:56.617 --> 00:04:58.825
Relevant means connected to the blank.

83
00:04:59.125 --> 00:05:02.419
A, door. B, topic. C, price.

84
00:05:05.967 --> 00:05:07.757
The answer is B: topic.

85
00:05:08.967 --> 00:05:12.292
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:15.173
How do you build a body paragraph?

87
00:05:23.983 --> 00:05:25.449
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:25.749 --> 00:05:37.332
I start with a clear point and add evidence such as a fact or an example. Then I explain why it matters. I use transitions like furthermore to connect my ideas.

89
00:05:37.632 --> 00:05:39.295
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:40.183 --> 00:05:44.299
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and point, evidence, explain.

91
00:05:44.599 --> 00:05:48.528
Today's value is thoroughness. Do the whole job, and do it well.

92
00:05:48.828 --> 00:05:51.771
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:52.071 --> 00:05:54.955
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

